  "worked_solution": "Splitting up the sum and factoring out the constants, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{3}({x}^{3}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{3}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{-1}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{4}\\,{|}_{-1}^{3}+4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{-1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}({3}^{4}-(-1)^{4})+2({3}^{2}-(-1)^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(81-1)+2(9-1) \\\\  & =20+16 \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
